  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- New module `crates/post/src/data_dir.rs`. It finds `assets/<kind>` at run time. The first directory that exists is used for the whole kind:\r\n  1. `<exe dir>/assets/<kind>` (zip, installer, Linux tarball, deb/rpm, AppImage, flatpak, snap)\r\n  2. `<app>/Contents/Resources/assets/<kind>` (macOS bundle)\r\n  3. `<exe dir>/../../assets/<kind>` (dev run from `target/<profile>/`)\r\n  4. `crates/post/../../assets/<kind>` (test binaries; a path, not a compiled-in copy)\r\n- Candidates 3 and 4 apply only when the exe is in a cargo build tree. The marker is cargo's `.fingerprint` folder in the exe folder, or in the folder above `deps` / `examples`. An installed exe without its `assets/<kind>` folder gets the named refusal. It never reads the build machine's checkout, `/usr/assets` or `C:/assets`.\r\n- There is no per-user `assets` folder. It could replace the shipped or repository files with no warning (review of this PR).\r\n- New file `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`. `BUILTINS` and `MACHINES` now hold the file name (`AssetFile`), not the text. `builtin_post_text`, `builtin_machine_text` and `default_mch_text` read each file one time into a static cell and give `&'static str`. There is no leak.\r\n- A missing directory, or a file that is missing, not UTF-8 or larger than 4 MiB, is an error. The error names the file and the directory. There is no compiled-in fallback on the desktop.\r\n- The `wasm32` build has no disk. It keeps a compiled-in copy.\r\n- Each read writes the full file path to the log one time. A user can see which post file made a program.\r\n- The callers in `posting.rs`, `posting_serves.rs`, `load_machine.rs`, `setup_mount.rs` and `machine/library.rs` use the new functions. The test files use them or `posting::shipped_posts()` / `posting::shipped_machines()`.\r\n- Themes: already read from disk (`crates/ui/src/theme_dir.rs`). No change.\r\n- Scripts: `assets/scripts` was never compiled in. No change.\r\n\r\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/2282-assets-from-disk.md`.\r\n\r\n## Packaging\r\n\r\nNo change to packaging, `build.rs` or workflows. The v0.22.0 Windows zip already has this layout:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncamcraft-0.22.0-win-x64/\r\n  assets/\r\n    machines/   (39 .mch)\r\n    posts/      (16 .cps)\r\n    scripts/\r\n    themes/\r\n    ui/\r\n  camcraft-cli.exe\r\n  camcraft-ui.exe\r\n  post.exe\r\n  LICENSE\r\n  NOTICE\r\n  RELEASE_NOTES.md\r\n  TESTING.md\r\n```\r\n\r\n`xtask/src/release_pack.rs` `ASSET_DIRS` and `scripts/package-*.sh` put the same `assets/` directories beside the executable on all platforms.\r\n\r\n## Readings and pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `camcraft-post` lib `data_dir::tests` (10 tests): order in a cargo tree, an installed exe without `assets` is refused (`an_installed_exe_without_assets_is_refused_not_redirected`), beside the exe wins, macOS bundle, missing directory error, missing file error, edited file loads and the read is cached, non-UTF-8 refusal, the 4 MiB cap (`a_file_over_the_size_cap_is_refused_by_name`), dev run finds the repository `assets`.\r\n- `camcraft-app` lib `posting::files::the_browser_list_matches_the_disk_tables`: each `BUILTINS` / `MACHINES` file and the default machine are in the `wasm32` `embedded()` list, with the same text as on disk.\r\n- `camcraft-app` `tests/shipped_from_disk.rs` (3 tests): each shipped post is the file on disk that `builtin_post_path` names; each machine reads; an unknown name is refused by name.\r\n- Review-fix head: `camcraft-post` lib 75 passed; `posting` 17 passed; `shipped_from_disk` 3 passed. The other binaries in this list passed on the first head and were not run again: `machine`, `machine_library`, `post_serves_kind`, `tinyg_post`, `grblhal_post`, `smoothing`, `explain_option`, `wire_post`, `sodick_alc400g`, `tormach_machines`, the `lathe_voice` lib tests.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean on the review-fix head.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The `wasm32` build: `flecs_ecs_sys` does not build for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` on this machine.\r\n- The other changed test binaries were compiled (clippy `--all-targets`) but not run. Their changes are mechanical lookups.\r\n- A packaged executable was not started.\r\n- The post dialog does not show the post file path yet. Follow-up: #2292.\r\n- Open PRs that add posts or machines to `posting.rs` (for example #2290, #2253, #2162) will conflict on the tables. Their new entries must use `AssetFile(\"<file>\")` and the `wasm32` `embedded` list. The test `the_browser_list_matches_the_disk_tables` fails if the list misses one.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The shipped post scripts and machine files are read from the assets folder beside the program at run time, so an edit there takes effect after a restart of the program, without a rebuild; a missing file is refused by name.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #2282\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
